From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] setup: make plain `build_ext` produce the amalgamation
 build

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [needed for our cibuildwheel-driven build, irrelevant to coleifer/pysqlite3]

setup.py maps the standard `build_ext` command to SystemLibSqliteBuilder
(dynamic link against the system libsqlite3) and only wires the
amalgamation-based, self-contained build in behind a custom `build_static`
command name. `pip wheel`/cibuildwheel never invoke `build_static` -- they
run the standard build_ext/bdist_wheel pipeline -- so without this change
our wheel would link dynamically against the manylinux image's ancient
libsqlite3 (no FTS5/JSON1) instead of the self-contained, fully-featured
build that is the entire point of the pysqlite3-binary distribution.
Point `build_ext` at AmalgationLibSqliteBuilder directly so a plain
`pip wheel .` (with sqlite3.c/sqlite3.h already fetched into the checkout
root) produces the intended self-contained extension.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 setup.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/setup.py b/setup.py
index a4b3c48..b143104 100644
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -154,7 +154,7 @@ def get_setup_args():
             "Topic :: Software Development :: Libraries :: Python Modules"],
         cmdclass={
             "build_static": AmalgationLibSqliteBuilder,
-            "build_ext": SystemLibSqliteBuilder
+            "build_ext": AmalgationLibSqliteBuilder
         }
     )
 
